[03:58:30] ## What changed
[03:58:30] **Resumed, not restarted.** The interrupted attempt had already written the calculator, JavaFX view, controller, DTO, four Java test classes and the three frontend files. I verified that work against the acceptance criteria rather than rewriting it, and **found one defect in it**: both browser smoke scripts had had their *expected* values renamed but not their *selectors* — `renderedScenarios` still read the removed `[data-test="ecto-scenario-dust-recovered"]` and the quote panel still read the two removed `dust-net-*` hooks. `npm run smoke:ecto` failed at step 3 with four `null` cells. I fixed both scripts; everything from there on — all verification and all documentation — is new.
[03:58:30] **The deduction.** `ecto.EctoSalvageCalculator` no longer owns a fee rate, multiplier or rounding rule (`SELL_FEE_PERCENT`, the private `0.85`, `netSaleProceeds(int)` are gone). It runs §46's order — yield first, fee second: `round(quote × 0.75)`, then `TradingPostFeePolicy.netOfFee(...)` once on that aggregate. At a 200c quote that reaches **127c** where the superseded per-unit order reached 128c. DOM-022's transaction primitive was deliberately not reused (§25.1), and `EctoSalvageService` needed no change at all.
[03:58:30] **Labels.** `dustNetUnitPrice` — a per-unit price *after* the fee, exactly the modeled sale §46 forbids — is replaced by the gross `expectedGrossRecoveredDustValue`. JavaFX quotes now say `(gross)`, both profitability titles say `after 15% TP fees`, and `fillProfitGrid` switched from `formatSigned` to `format`: `formatSigned` calls `format(Math.abs(copper))`, so all four cells had been rendering salvage losses as gains.
[03:58:30] ## Tests
[03:58:30] - `./mvnw test -Dtest='EctoSalvageCalculatorTest,EctoSalvageServiceTest,EctoSalvageApiControllerTest'` — **Tests run: 30, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, BUILD SUCCESS**
[03:58:30] - `./mvnw test -Dtest=EctoSalvageViewIT` — **Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, BUILD SUCCESS** (local TestFX, real desktop)
[03:58:30] - `npx vitest run src/ecto` — **21 passed**; `type-check` and `build` clean
[03:58:30] - `npm run smoke:ecto` — **PASSED, 10 steps** (real Chrome, stub origin `127.0.0.1:5182`)
[03:58:30] - `npm run smoke:ecto:live` — **PASSED** against the real backend and live Trading Post. I checked the served body by hand against §46: quote 1023c gross → `767c` expected gross recovered → `115c` fee → `652c` net → `1143c` net cost → `-11s 43c` rendered → `57 150c` per 1000 Luck.
[03:58:30] For the live run the backend and a dedicated dev server were started fresh (the DTO had changed), the dev server bound to `--host 127.0.0.1` after the first attempt confirmed Vite's default bind answers on `::1` only, and afterwards only this session's own process trees were killed — a pre-existing four-day-old `spring-boot:run` tree was left alone — with `curl` confirming both ports released.
[03:58:30] Docs updated: `CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` (six places), `KNOWN_PROBLEMS.md` KP-09, `docs/crafting/README.md`. `DOMAIN_SPEC.md` already specified this rule exactly, so the implementation moved to the spec, not the reverse.
[03:58:30] Two follow-up findings recorded (`formatSigned` still losing signs in both crafting views, plus a no-op ternary at `CraftingProfitView.java:909`; and the smoke scripts accepting a stale `dist/`). No accuracy or milestone-completion claim is made.
