[04:40:36] - New `assertMeasured(samples, required, where)` runs before the sample-count floor and fails when a required pair is absent, when no `sample` call produced that name (a rename the in-browser side can't detect), or when its ratio isn't finite.
[04:40:36] - New step 7 is the negative control: it removes the rendered `[data-test="page-intro"]` (asserting the removal took effect first), re-measures, requires an empty set, and requires `assertMeasured` to throw naming the pair. Step 8 reloads Crafting Profit so the removal can't leak.
[04:40:36] - Preserved unchanged: contrast math, all sixteen selectors, the probed status tones, thresholds, the `>= 15` floor, the display filters, steps 1–5. `only` defaults to `null`.
